# Test: an SCCRQ that omits an AVP RFC 2661 Section 6.1 makes mandatory is
# answered with StopCCN.
#
# VALIDATES: the daemon refuses an SCCRQ that is missing a required AVP, on the
#            path a peer drives, and keeps accepting a complete SCCRQ on the
#            same socket. Every octet is read off a real UDP datagram by a
#            native Go fixture decoder that shares no code with ze.
# PREVENTS:  the establishment this test was written for. Until this change
#            parseSCCRQ checked no Protocol Version and no Framing Capabilities
#            presence, so an SCCRQ carrying neither brought the tunnel up with
#            a framing mask of 0 -- a zero standing in for an answer, and a
#            peer told nothing.
#
# Why unit evidence cannot reach this obligation: the unit tests in
# internal/component/l2tp/reactor_sccrq_mandatory_avp_test.go read the reply
# with ze's own parseStopCCN, so an encoder and a decoder that share a
# misreading agree with each other. Here the Result Code, the Error Code and
# the Error Message are unpacked with encoding/binary against values written
# out of the RFC.
#
# Both polarities run against one daemon, so neither can pass because the
# listener was down.
#
# RFC requirement: RFC2661-6.1-1 negative -- an SCCRQ carrying no Framing
# Capabilities AVP is answered with a StopCCN whose Result Code is 2, whose
# Error Code is 3 and whose Error Message names that AVP, read off the wire by
# a decoder that is not ze.
# RFC requirement: RFC2661-6.1-1 positive -- an SCCRQ carrying all five AVPs of
# Section 6.1 gets SCCRP on the same path, addressed with the peer's Assigned
# Tunnel ID.


stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
l2tp {
	enabled true
}
environment {
	l2tp {
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1
			port $PORT
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

option=env:var=ze.log.l2tp:value=debug
option=env:var=ze.l2tp.skip-kernel-probe:value=true

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=config
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze-test fixture l2tp/rfc2661-sccrq-mandatory-avp $PORT:timeout=20s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: all RFC 2661 SCCRQ mandatory AVP checks passed
# The daemon's own record that it chose to answer rather than drop, and that it
# named the AVP. A positive signal, so the reply cannot have come from some
# other path.
expect=stderr:contains=malformed SCCRQ answered with StopCCN
expect=stderr:contains=SCCRQ missing Framing Capabilities AVP
# And the positive polarity reached the tunnel machinery rather than stopping
# at the parser.
expect=stderr:contains=new tunnel created from SCCRQ
